## Before Working

1. Read `docs/PLAYBOOK.md` — session entry point, identifies active lifecycle phase
2. If in execution phase: Read `docs/CURRENT_WORK.md` → `context/WORKING.md` → Phase SPEC.md
3. Sync: `git fetch origin && git log --oneline HEAD..origin/$(git branch --show-current) | head -5`

## TDD Gate (Non-Negotiable)

**No code without scenarios. No scenarios without acceptance criteria.**

| Step | Output | Gate |
|-|-|-|
| 1. Plan | SPEC.md + SCENARIOS.md | Planning outputs exist |
| 2. RED | Scenario runs and FAILS | Failure = correct (missing impl) |
| 3. GREEN | Implementation code, scenario PASSES | `{{ type_check_command }}` passes |
| 4. VALIDATE | acceptance checks pass: every scenario executed, type check and build green | Hard block on missing scenarios |

Runtime-specific commands for these steps are mapped in `CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code); other runtimes run the checks directly.

**Scope classification:**

| Trigger (ANY match) | Scope | TDD Required? |
|-|-|-|
| New DB tables/columns | Standard+ | Yes |
| New API routes | Standard+ | Yes |
| New UI pages/major components | Standard+ | Yes |
| 4+ files modified | Standard+ | Yes |
| Single-file bug fix, no new surface area | Quick | No |

## Work Routing

| Source | Route |
|-|-|
| Quick fix (single-file, no new surface area) | Fix → Commit with `Fixes #N` |
| Standard+ (see TDD Gate scope triggers) | SPEC → SCENARIOS → RED → GREEN → VALIDATE |
| External concern | Append to `context/DISCOVERIES.md` → keep working |

For dispatch/handoff summaries and scoped evidence comparison, use `docs/DELIVERY.md`.
It consolidates the work reference; existing entry, review and effect gates still apply.

## Skills

Canonical skills live in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (Codex reads them there); `.claude/skills/<name>/` is
the byte-identical generated projection for Claude Code — never edit the projection by hand. Before implementing
20+ lines, invoke the matching best-practices skill; if a skill's information is wrong or outdated, update the skill
immediately.

Before using `ponytail` or `caveman`, read `docs/SKILL_MODES.md` and apply the mode it sets for your
responsibility. Upstream defaults do not apply: `caveman` runs `lite` for routine updates and never compresses
exact facts, code, errors, numbers, ordering, requested detail, warnings, handoffs, verdicts or records; `ponytail`
narrows implementations, never requirements, evidence or gates.

## Development Protocol

For each PROGRESS.md item: implement → check off → commit. If exit landmarks met → Signal `[PHASE_COMPLETE]`.

